VulkanRender - reusable C++17 VulkanWrapper rendering.
  render/render.hpp         umbrella API
  render/frame.*            two+ in-flight command/fence and present scheduler
  render/postprocess.*      owned offscreen HDR/LDR targets and presentation pass
  render/pipeline.*         graphics pipeline creation from SPIR-V
  render/target.*           arbitrary color/depth render pass and framebuffer
  render/mesh.hpp           non-owning vertex and index views
  render/geometry.hpp       GPU vertex/index buffer ownership and batch uploads
  render/attachments.hpp    generic sampled render-target image/view ownership
  render/sequence.hpp       ordered render/compute passes on gpu::graph
  render/material.hpp       non-owning descriptor and push-constant bindings
  render/renderer.*         pass, indexed/indirect draw helpers
  render/camera.hpp         optional camera payload
  render/light.hpp          optional light payload

frame_scheduler.create(frames), resize(swapchain image count), wait(), begin(),
then render to ticket.command and submit(ticket). Handle out-of-date/suboptimal
swapchain results in the host and recreate resources only after device idle.
The host owns surface creation, format/present-mode choice and VulkanWrapper
lifecycle. It also controls shader semantics, camera, lighting and passes.

postprocess_targets creates sampled/storage HDR and LDR GPU images and views
per swapchain image. presentation_targets constructs the swapchain-compatible
pass and framebuffers; the caller supplies shaders, descriptor sets, and effects.

Geometry buffers, attachment images and cross-pass barriers belong here.
No fixed vertex layout, tonemapper, lighting implementation, or game semantics.
GPU work referencing a render target must complete before its owner resets.


